MiniGPT — From Tokens to Language
Educational project published by Thinking About Data.

Acknowledgments and provenance
This project is inspired by Sebastian Raschka, Build a Large Language Model
(From Scratch), Manning, 2024, and its official code repository:
https://github.com/rasbt/LLMs-from-scratch
Upstream license: https://github.com/rasbt/LLMs-from-scratch/blob/main/LICENSE.txt

MiniGPT is a simplified implementation developed for a Polish educational
blog series, with AI-assisted code preparation. It is not an official fork,
product, or endorsed implementation of Sebastian Raschka or OpenAI.
Differences include PyTorch's built-in MultiheadAttention and LayerNorm,
a smaller configuration, a simplified dataset and training workflow,
and training on Polish literature without pretrained GPT-2 weights.

The upstream software license is Apache 2.0, with an explicit exclusion
for books and related images. No book prose, illustrations, or pretrained
weights are distributed here. Any upstream notices applicable to reused
code must be retained. Third-party dependencies retain their own licenses.
